WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.301 --> 00:00:02.635
-My first guest
is a Grammy-winning artist

00:00:02.635 --> 00:00:04.870
with a brand-new single out.
It is awesome.

00:00:04.870 --> 00:00:07.306
It's called
"Let Me Reintroduce Myself."

00:00:07.306 --> 00:00:09.075
It went straight to number one.

00:00:09.075 --> 00:00:13.279
Here she is -- Gwen Stefani!
Aw, Come on!

00:00:13.279 --> 00:00:15.214
-Whoo!
-Yay!

00:00:15.214 --> 00:00:17.417
-Gwen --
-I can't believe I'm back.

00:00:17.417 --> 00:00:20.553
-I love it. Dude,
I want you back every week.

00:00:20.553 --> 00:00:21.888
-Aww, thank you.

00:00:21.888 --> 00:00:23.056
-I don't know
if you remember this.

00:00:23.056 --> 00:00:25.391
A few years ago,
you gave me a suggestion

00:00:25.391 --> 00:00:28.261
for my girls
for Christmas morning to --

00:00:28.261 --> 00:00:29.996
-Yes.
-To put Christmas wrapping

00:00:29.996 --> 00:00:33.299
on the doorway on their way
into the tree

00:00:33.299 --> 00:00:36.235
so that they rip it open
and then see the presents.

00:00:36.235 --> 00:00:39.271
Is that right?
-But obviously Santa

00:00:39.271 --> 00:00:42.441
and the elves do that.
You have to e-mail him,

00:00:42.441 --> 00:00:45.011
and then he does that,
if you request it, yep?

00:00:45.011 --> 00:00:47.079
-So I requested it.
I talked to Santa.

00:00:47.079 --> 00:00:52.051
Santa put on the paper on the --
wrapped the door so beautifully.

00:00:52.051 --> 00:00:53.519
And I was, like --
Oh, it was so cool.

00:00:53.519 --> 00:00:55.955
I couldn't believe it.
I was in shock when I woke up.

00:00:55.955 --> 00:00:59.025
In the morning.
And I go down to videotape

00:00:59.025 --> 00:01:00.593
on the other side,
because I want my girls

00:01:00.593 --> 00:01:03.195
to run in and rip --
But there's just such --

00:01:03.195 --> 00:01:06.031
I mean, you have boys,
so you --

00:01:06.031 --> 00:01:07.867
I have girls, and they came in,

00:01:07.867 --> 00:01:10.770
and they politely just pushed it
open like it's a curtain.

00:01:10.770 --> 00:01:12.705
-No!
-Yeah, and it was such a --

00:01:12.705 --> 00:01:16.175
-They didn't crash through it?
-They're so polite.

00:01:16.175 --> 00:01:18.043
They just pushed
like it was a curtain.

00:01:18.043 --> 00:01:20.479
And they're so excited
'cause Santa came.

00:01:20.479 --> 00:01:22.582
But they didn't rip it
or anything.

00:01:22.582 --> 00:01:26.719
It's like, "I have to take
a picture and send it to Gwen,"

00:01:26.719 --> 00:01:29.388
because it's the best idea,
honestly,

00:01:29.388 --> 00:01:31.490
and everyone should ask Santa
if they can do this.

00:01:31.490 --> 00:01:34.593
But I ended up cutting a hole
in the Christmas wrapping,

00:01:34.593 --> 00:01:37.063
and just sticking my daughter's
head in the doorway.

00:01:37.063 --> 00:01:39.232
-Oh, my God!
[ Both laugh ]

00:01:39.232 --> 00:01:41.066
-Because she wouldn't rip it.
-That is so cute.

00:01:41.066 --> 00:01:42.535
-That's the only rip
is that right there.

00:01:42.535 --> 00:01:46.473
They just pushed it open.
-Oh, my gosh.

00:01:46.473 --> 00:01:49.775
-Well, I feel like you have
to take that same picture now

00:01:49.775 --> 00:01:51.777
every single year,
'cause that's what we do.

00:01:51.777 --> 00:01:53.913
We always have a picture,
like, in front of the paper.

00:01:53.913 --> 00:01:56.415
And we were at a new house.
We moved.

00:01:56.415 --> 00:01:58.485
So it was, like,
a really big deal this year

00:01:58.485 --> 00:02:01.488
'cause we didn't know, like,
where Santa was gonna actually

00:02:01.488 --> 00:02:04.690
wrap the opening 'cause it's,
like, a really big opening.

00:02:04.690 --> 00:02:06.959
-Oh, my goodness.
-And ours was crashed through

00:02:06.959 --> 00:02:10.296
by, like, teenager
and, like, littles.

00:02:10.296 --> 00:02:12.765
It was fun.
-I want to congratulate you

00:02:12.765 --> 00:02:16.602
because you and Blake Shelton
are engaged!

00:02:16.602 --> 00:02:18.504
Come on!
-Yay!

00:02:18.504 --> 00:02:21.407
-That's what I'm talking about.
I love it.

00:02:21.407 --> 00:02:24.243
I have questions.
How did Blake propose?

00:02:24.243 --> 00:02:27.247
Did he have it all planned out?
What was it like?

00:02:27.247 --> 00:02:30.015
-Well, um, it was actually
pretty magical.

00:02:30.015 --> 00:02:35.121
And wasn't expecting it at the
moment that it happened at all.

00:02:35.121 --> 00:02:37.089
Didn't have any idea.
Nobody knew.

00:02:37.089 --> 00:02:39.926
I think he had told my dad
on my birthday

00:02:39.926 --> 00:02:43.596
about two weeks earlier.
And I got to tell you, like,

00:02:43.596 --> 00:02:45.698
I was sort of like,
"What's happening with us?"

00:02:45.698 --> 00:02:48.535
Like, it was kind of in my mind,
"Like, we've been together

00:02:48.535 --> 00:02:51.570
a long time now.
Like, what's going on?"

00:02:51.570 --> 00:02:54.206
I was in that place in my head.

00:02:54.206 --> 00:02:57.744
And we also had this trip
planned to come on Oklahoma,

00:02:57.744 --> 00:03:00.779
and it was one of those COVID
kind of, like, not a fight,

00:03:00.779 --> 00:03:03.750
but it was like, "Maybe we
should just cancel the trip."

00:03:03.750 --> 00:03:06.051
Like, "This is getting too hard.
Like, it's not gonna --"

00:03:06.051 --> 00:03:08.554
Everybody has to get tested,
and everyone was on edge,

00:03:08.554 --> 00:03:10.756
'cause we were gonna meet up
with his sister

00:03:10.756 --> 00:03:12.224
and brother-in-law
and their family.

00:03:12.224 --> 00:03:15.828
And everything, all the plans,
you can't make plans anymore.

00:03:15.828 --> 00:03:19.432
So, anyways, we were this close
to, like, canceling the trip.

00:03:19.432 --> 00:03:22.768
And we ended up
making it all happen.

00:03:22.768 --> 00:03:24.404
And we were all here
at the ranch,

00:03:24.404 --> 00:03:26.439
and, basically, it happened.

00:03:26.439 --> 00:03:28.975
But it was like everybody was
trying to make it not happen

00:03:28.975 --> 00:03:30.742
'cause nobody knew
it was gonna happen.

00:03:30.742 --> 00:03:33.846
And Blake, meanwhile,
had this ring, like, I guess,

00:03:33.846 --> 00:03:35.681
in the side of his, like, truck.

00:03:35.681 --> 00:03:37.249
And when I say
"the side of his truck,"

00:03:37.249 --> 00:03:41.153
like, his truck is disgusting.
It is like things falling out,

00:03:41.153 --> 00:03:44.791
like, equipment,
like total rugged man stuff.

00:03:44.791 --> 00:03:46.091
-Yeah.
Like, mud, you know?

00:03:46.091 --> 00:03:48.161
-He got mad at me that
there's no mud on my truck.

00:03:48.161 --> 00:03:50.195
He goes, "Jimmy, don't ever
show me that truck."

00:03:50.195 --> 00:03:51.930
'Cause I showed him a picture
of my truck, and it was like --

00:03:51.930 --> 00:03:53.899
There's not even any --
"I can't even look at it.

00:03:53.899 --> 00:03:56.335
There's no mud on that truck.
You have to use that."

00:03:56.335 --> 00:03:57.736
He was so disappointed.
-I know.

00:03:57.736 --> 00:03:59.539
-So I can imagine
what his truck looks like.

00:03:59.539 --> 00:04:02.074
It's a real ranch truck.
-Yes.

00:04:02.074 --> 00:04:04.877
And there's, like,
a lot of junk in it and dirt.

00:04:04.877 --> 00:04:06.312
And so the fact
that the ring was, like,

00:04:06.312 --> 00:04:07.480
in the side of the door --

00:04:07.480 --> 00:04:10.083
And, like, you're driving
through trees and stuff.

00:04:10.083 --> 00:04:12.785
Like, it could just like
fall out at any point.

00:04:12.785 --> 00:04:15.188
-Oh, my gosh.
-Anyways, it was pretty magical.

00:04:15.188 --> 00:04:18.558
And my brother was trying to
cook like a hobo stew at home,

00:04:18.558 --> 00:04:19.759
so he was like,
"We gotta get back!

00:04:19.759 --> 00:04:21.093
It's gonna burn!"

00:04:21.093 --> 00:04:23.162
And my son was, like,
"I gotta go to the bathroom!"

00:04:23.162 --> 00:04:25.531
And, like,
nobody wanted to be there.

00:04:25.531 --> 00:04:29.168
Anyways, out of nowhere,
he just has this ring

00:04:29.168 --> 00:04:31.070
that's, like,
in a cabinet when I opened it.

00:04:31.070 --> 00:04:32.839
He's like,
"Oh, get the fire starter,"

00:04:32.839 --> 00:04:35.307
and I, like, open the cabinet,
and there's this ring there.

00:04:35.307 --> 00:04:36.876
And I'm like,
"Are you serious?!"

00:04:36.876 --> 00:04:38.944
[ Chuckles ]
It was pretty, like, "What?!"

00:04:38.944 --> 00:04:41.848
And we both start bawling,
and everyone was in shock.

00:04:41.848 --> 00:04:45.117
There was no video.
My sister-in-law-to-be

00:04:45.117 --> 00:04:47.153
was there, and she just started,
like, shooting off pictures,

00:04:47.153 --> 00:04:49.688
and that's the shot
that we put out.

00:04:49.688 --> 00:04:53.159
It was just a random picture.
So, it is pretty exciting.

00:04:53.159 --> 00:04:54.326
-It's kind of fun
not having it on video.

00:04:54.326 --> 00:04:56.828
-We have no plans
because of the pandemic.

00:04:56.828 --> 00:04:59.866
It's like, "Blake, why couldn't
you have done it before?

00:04:59.866 --> 00:05:01.734
Now we can't have a wedding
with the pandemic."

00:05:01.734 --> 00:05:04.603
-[ Laughing ]
-Sitting around going, "Okay."

00:05:04.603 --> 00:05:06.773
Drag it out more.
-You guys are so famous,

00:05:06.773 --> 00:05:08.541
it was actually good news
for the world,

00:05:08.541 --> 00:05:10.843
'cause we all needed -- any good
news, and we'll take it.

00:05:10.843 --> 00:05:13.979
And I was like, "Yes!"
We all cheered.

00:05:13.979 --> 00:05:15.948
So just know it was awesome.
Congratulations.

00:05:15.948 --> 00:05:17.183
-Thank you.
Thank you so much.

00:05:17.183 --> 00:05:19.651
-And tell Blake
he's a hopeless romantic.

00:05:19.651 --> 00:05:21.687
I've got to talk to him
about that truck move.

00:05:21.687 --> 00:05:25.157
Let's talk about
"Let Me Reintroduce Myself."

00:05:25.157 --> 00:05:27.593
Came out last month,
went straight to number one.

00:05:27.593 --> 00:05:30.496
Congrats on this.
-Thank you.

00:05:30.496 --> 00:05:32.098
-This is the perfect song,
by the way.

00:05:32.098 --> 00:05:35.367
-Thank you, thank you.
-And the video,

00:05:35.367 --> 00:05:38.671
how'd you come up with the idea
to do all of your looks?

00:05:38.671 --> 00:05:42.107
-Well, this is --
Basically, it wasn't my idea.

00:05:42.107 --> 00:05:43.675
I had --
We were doing that song,

00:05:43.675 --> 00:05:45.478
"Happy Anywhere," me and Blake.

00:05:45.478 --> 00:05:47.446
And we were here
in the pandemic, stuck,

00:05:47.446 --> 00:05:50.249
quarantined at the ranch,
so we didn't get a chance

00:05:50.249 --> 00:05:53.419
to do, like, a real video.
My brother happened to be here,

00:05:53.419 --> 00:05:55.721
and so we kind of
made the video that we made.

00:05:55.721 --> 00:05:58.190
But my original idea
for that video was,

00:05:58.190 --> 00:06:01.227
"You be Blake from the '90s,
like with a mullet,

00:06:01.227 --> 00:06:04.129
and I'll be me,
the 'Just a Girl' me,

00:06:04.129 --> 00:06:06.933
and we could, like, be the
different versions of us

00:06:06.933 --> 00:06:09.334
in this video,
like, happy anywhere.

00:06:09.334 --> 00:06:11.970
Like, this weird couple
that doesn't make any sense,

00:06:11.970 --> 00:06:13.806
but we do.
-Ah.

00:06:13.806 --> 00:06:16.108
-And he was not into it.
But we could've never done it

00:06:16.108 --> 00:06:18.711
anyways because we were
stuck here at the ranch.

00:06:18.711 --> 00:06:21.480
Anyways, Blake was the one
that said, "You know, that song,

00:06:21.480 --> 00:06:25.351
'Let Me Reintroduce Myself,'
that's a hit," or whatever.

00:06:25.351 --> 00:06:28.554
And because he has had like
27 number-one radio hits,

00:06:28.554 --> 00:06:31.624
and he's been on "The Voice"
for 20 seasons picking songs

00:06:31.624 --> 00:06:34.259
and being around music,
I trust him in that.

00:06:34.259 --> 00:06:36.261
And he was the one who said,
"You should, like --"

00:06:36.261 --> 00:06:38.531
He called me
driving to the airport

00:06:38.531 --> 00:06:40.933
and was like,
"You should dress up as you

00:06:40.933 --> 00:06:43.335
in all your old looks
and do this video."

00:06:43.335 --> 00:06:46.371
And I was, like, "Whoa. That's
actually a really good idea."

00:06:46.371 --> 00:06:47.840
-I mean,
look at all these looks.

00:06:47.840 --> 00:06:50.443
It's genius.
Gwen, I'm telling you,

00:06:50.443 --> 00:06:52.444
it was just --
-Wow.

00:06:52.444 --> 00:06:54.146
-I just love
that you did all this.

00:06:54.146 --> 00:06:56.315
It's so fantastic.
-It was so much work.

00:06:56.315 --> 00:06:59.485
It was so fun, though,
but it was really trippy,

00:06:59.485 --> 00:07:02.989
because, like,
you would basically --

00:07:02.989 --> 00:07:06.191
It'd be in the original look
of what I was back then,

00:07:06.191 --> 00:07:08.127
and it brought back
so many memories.

00:07:08.127 --> 00:07:10.663
And I never thought,
when I was doing those looks,

00:07:10.663 --> 00:07:13.332
that I would be basically
a Halloween costume

00:07:13.332 --> 00:07:14.900
to other people.
-[ Laughs ]

00:07:14.900 --> 00:07:17.302
Like, that was actually
how I dressed,

00:07:17.302 --> 00:07:19.839
not because anyone told me to,
but that was like --

00:07:19.839 --> 00:07:22.441
I had that polka-dot dress
in my closet forever.

00:07:22.441 --> 00:07:27.246
And just the fact that
they became so recognizable,

00:07:27.246 --> 00:07:29.014
it was really fun to revisit it.

00:07:29.014 --> 00:07:32.184
And it was just
a really fun way to come back.

00:07:32.184 --> 00:07:34.887
-Is there an album on the way,
or is this just a tease?

00:07:34.887 --> 00:07:36.588
-Yes, of course.
-There is?

00:07:36.588 --> 00:07:37.990
-I mean, that was --
I mean, at first,

00:07:37.990 --> 00:07:40.826
I didn't know
if I would do an album or not.

00:07:40.826 --> 00:07:43.395
But I have all these songs,
and I think that even, like,

00:07:43.395 --> 00:07:45.597
next week, I want to go back in
and start writing again

00:07:45.597 --> 00:07:47.933
because I don't feel like
I'm quite done writing.

00:07:47.933 --> 00:07:52.070
And I think the writing process
has been incredibly exciting.

00:07:52.070 --> 00:07:54.574
I mean, I love writing.
That's my favorite thing to do.

